🚽 Test case: issue #278 -- unary arithmetic negation of a smol (short)
🚽 computed logical NOT instead of arithmetic negation.
🚽
🚽 In handle_unary_expression() (ast.c), the OP_NEG case had a copy-paste error
🚽 in the VAR_SHORT arm using `!` instead of `-`. Consequently, -x collapsed to
🚽 0 for any non-zero value and 1 for 0.
🚽
🚽 This fixture tests:
🚽 1. Negation of positive smol: -5
🚽 2. Negation of zero smol: 0 (not 1)
🚽 3. Negation of negative smol: 5
🚽 4. Double negation: -(-5) = 5
🚽 5. Boundary value (SHRT_MAX = 32767): -32767
🚽 6. Assignment of negated smol to smol variable: -5
🚽 7. Parity with rizz (int) negation: -5

skibidi main {
    smol a = 5;
    yapping("%d", -a);

    smol c = 0;
    yapping("%d", -c);

    smol neg = -5;
    yapping("%d", -neg);

    yapping("%d", -(-a));

    smol max_val = 32767;
    yapping("%d", -max_val);

    smol res = -a;
    yapping("%d", res);

    rizz r = 5;
    yapping("%d", -r);

    bussin 0;
}
